WEBVTT

00:20.000 --> 00:24.540
<b>SPY CLASSROOM</b>

01:31.540 --> 01:38.380
<b>FILE: Lamplight Days</b>

01:33.290 --> 01:35.080
Heat Haze Palace...

01:35.080 --> 01:37.170
It's unclear how true it is,

01:37.170 --> 01:40.330
but it's said that the manor was once a hideout
belonging to the royal family

01:40.330 --> 01:43.040
and was a palace in every sense of the word.

01:43.040 --> 01:47.880
<b>During the Pre-Impossible Mission Training</b>

01:44.630 --> 01:47.130
Nowadays, though...

01:50.500 --> 01:53.540
Nothing works!

01:54.920 --> 01:56.380
Not at all.

01:56.380 --> 01:59.130
Your wire trap today was well-executed.

01:59.380 --> 02:01.250
I could feel your training paying off.

02:04.580 --> 02:05.920
Hooray?

02:05.920 --> 02:06.920
Yes.

02:07.290 --> 02:08.500
However,

02:08.500 --> 02:12.920
the fact you aren't being as elegant and graceful as
a seafowl's plumage as it soars through a zephyr

02:12.920 --> 02:14.250
is really kind of disappointing.

02:14.250 --> 02:16.210
I didn't follow a word of that...

02:16.210 --> 02:18.880
...but I could tell he was saying
we fell short of the mark.

02:20.040 --> 02:22.880
We really are washouts, aren't we?

02:22.880 --> 02:25.290
We've already been here for over ten days.

02:25.290 --> 02:27.710
But every day, we keep losing!

02:27.710 --> 02:28.920
We suck, yo!

02:28.920 --> 02:31.290
At this rate, we're done for.

02:31.630 --> 02:33.290
Don't be so hard on yourselves.

02:33.290 --> 02:35.710
All of you are getting stronger.

02:36.080 --> 02:38.750
I'm just so powerful it's hard to tell, that's all.

02:39.500 --> 02:41.170
I'll be looking forward to your next attack.

02:41.170 --> 02:43.420
Hey! At least untie the damn wires!

02:43.630 --> 02:45.210
Undo them yourselves.

02:45.210 --> 02:46.630
Consider it part of your training.

02:47.250 --> 02:48.500
How unlucky...

02:49.750 --> 02:53.380
Whoa, the wires didn't leave a single mark.

02:53.380 --> 02:54.830
I guess that's a professional for you.

02:54.830 --> 02:56.670
Color me surprised.

02:56.670 --> 03:00.670
I never figured a meathead gorilla like you
would care about that kind of stuff.

03:00.670 --> 03:02.330
Who you callin' a gorilla?

03:02.330 --> 03:04.130
If I had to pick someone...

03:05.040 --> 03:07.750
You would have expected me
to be the one who was concerned?

03:08.290 --> 03:10.790
I mean, seduction is her area of expertise.

03:10.790 --> 03:12.000
Honestly, I wasn't too worried.

03:12.000 --> 03:16.000
There are plenty of men who get turned on
by rope burns and such in the bedroom.

03:16.790 --> 03:20.960
You know, for someone who likes to play the cynic,
you're actually surprisingly childish.

03:20.960 --> 03:22.000
Excuse me? I'll have you know I-

03:22.000 --> 03:23.290
L-let's just drop it, okay?

03:23.290 --> 03:25.460
I can't stand it when conversations get all raunchy!

03:25.460 --> 03:26.710
Wait, for real?

03:26.710 --> 03:29.670
More importantly, what should we
do for our next attack?

03:29.920 --> 03:34.080
I've been giving it some thought,
and I say we all head into town together and-

03:35.290 --> 03:36.750
Yeah, about that.

03:36.750 --> 03:40.040
There's no reason to be so fixated
on working as a group.

03:41.130 --> 03:42.330
She's right.

03:42.330 --> 03:44.790
It might be a good idea for us each
to try our own thing for a bit.

03:44.790 --> 03:45.790
I agree.

03:45.790 --> 03:49.710
There isn't any rule that says
we always have to attack him as a team.

03:50.080 --> 03:51.960
You cool with that, Leader?

03:59.790 --> 04:01.210
The bath's all yours.

04:01.210 --> 04:02.420
Roger that, yo!

04:02.420 --> 04:05.250
The younger group will head on in, then.

04:05.540 --> 04:07.130
C'mon, let's have a contest!

04:07.130 --> 04:08.880
We'll see who can stay underwater the longest!

04:08.880 --> 04:11.210
I wanted to take my bath alone...

04:11.960 --> 04:14.750
I see, that's what you were talking about in the bath.

04:14.960 --> 04:15.960
Yeah.

04:15.960 --> 04:20.330
I know it's not a rule or anything,
but we don't have long before the Impossible Mission.

04:20.330 --> 04:24.290
You would think that developing our teamwork
would be priority number one.

04:24.580 --> 04:28.170
We were able to work together with
some success the other day,

04:28.170 --> 04:32.290
but that doesn't change the fact that Lamplight is
an ad hoc team that only just came together.

04:38.380 --> 04:40.750
And what's more, many of us have loud personalities.

04:40.750 --> 04:44.420
Getting us all on the same page
will be easier said than done.

04:47.500 --> 04:49.750
Getting in some solo training at this hour?

04:50.080 --> 04:52.290
Your efforts are commendable, Sybilla.

04:52.750 --> 04:54.920
I mean, I guess...

04:56.380 --> 04:58.420
This is a problem.

04:58.420 --> 05:00.960
As the team leader, what's a girl to do?

05:01.710 --> 05:05.130
We need to talk, Leader.

05:05.500 --> 05:06.710
Huh?

05:08.790 --> 05:11.960
Wow, this is what your room looks like?

05:11.960 --> 05:14.130
The furnishings are all so nice!

05:14.460 --> 05:15.460
They're all right.

05:15.460 --> 05:19.960
I was hoping to get the corner room,
but you went and snatched it up first.

05:19.960 --> 05:23.080
Look, I won that lottery fair and square-

05:23.080 --> 05:24.420
While I have you...

05:25.380 --> 05:27.290
I must say, I'm shocked.

05:27.290 --> 05:31.290
To think that you, of all people,
would be such a late bloomer.

05:32.290 --> 05:34.960
Whether or not you have any actual experience,

05:34.960 --> 05:39.250
your academy should have at least
taught you the basics of seduction.

05:39.290 --> 05:41.500
I would have assumed it was right up your alley.

05:41.500 --> 05:44.040
You have a cunning streak a mile long
and a heart devoid of shame.

05:44.040 --> 05:46.880
Fl-flattery will get you nowhere, you know!

05:46.880 --> 05:48.920
Ah, what a waste.

05:49.330 --> 05:51.710
You even have the perfect assets for the job.

05:51.710 --> 05:53.960
Oh, this will do just fine.

05:54.500 --> 05:57.290
I'm going to give you a makeover, Lily.

05:57.290 --> 06:01.080
What do you say to taking Teach down
with some seduction?

06:01.710 --> 06:06.330
Men like him tend to go for the bashful, innocent type

06:06.330 --> 06:08.830
over more confident women like me.

06:09.040 --> 06:12.130
That flirtatious blush you're going for
right now is perfect.

06:12.130 --> 06:13.880
I'm not going for anything!

06:13.880 --> 06:15.080
I'm really not!

06:16.290 --> 06:19.710
Think of how impressed we would be
if you got Teach to surrender.

06:19.710 --> 06:23.540
"That's our leader for you!" we'd all say.

06:24.130 --> 06:25.420
Y-you can talk it up all you like-

06:25.420 --> 06:26.670
You'll do it for us, won't you...

06:27.830 --> 06:29.040
Leader?

06:37.460 --> 06:38.670
Come in.

06:39.500 --> 06:41.080
S-so, um...

06:48.460 --> 06:50.540
I need your help, Big Brother!

06:50.540 --> 06:51.750
"Big Brother"?

06:51.750 --> 06:56.920
I just remembered that I
was your little sister in a past life.

06:57.040 --> 07:03.330
I-I was also a maid who loved serving you,

07:03.330 --> 07:08.790
and every night, I would give you a massage
to ease your fatigue, just the two of us.

07:09.040 --> 07:11.130
Now, come on, lie down!

07:11.790 --> 07:13.380
Also, if you drink this before I start,

07:13.380 --> 07:17.830
it will make the massage twice as effective, meow!

07:21.500 --> 07:25.630
Lily, how much longer should
I keep playing along with this game?

07:26.420 --> 07:29.040
If there's something troubling you,
I'd be happy to lend you an ear.

07:35.170 --> 07:39.130
Please just forget this ever happened!

07:44.380 --> 07:46.630
That sounds pretty rough.

07:46.630 --> 07:48.830
That's why I told her I didn't want to do it!

07:48.830 --> 07:51.540
What about Miss Thea?
What did she say?

07:51.540 --> 07:53.830
Oh, get a load of this!

07:54.210 --> 07:56.170
Well, I expected about as much.

07:56.170 --> 07:58.460
I have to say, that man has the self-control of a monk.

07:58.460 --> 08:01.040
It's all but unthinkable, from a man of his age.

08:01.040 --> 08:03.710
Actually, how old is Teach?

08:04.080 --> 08:07.630
Thank you for the valuable data, Leader.

08:07.830 --> 08:09.210
She's the worst!

08:09.210 --> 08:11.460
I didn't want to go along, but seduction is her specialty,

08:11.460 --> 08:13.580
so I figured she knew what she was-

08:15.210 --> 08:20.420
It's only the inside of the manor that's bugged,
so I think you're fine.

08:20.710 --> 08:21.920
R-right...

08:22.290 --> 08:27.170
That aside, it's nice how you young'uns
are working together so well.

08:27.380 --> 08:31.750
I think Erna and Annette
really hit it off the other day.

08:31.750 --> 08:33.330
I wouldn't be so sure...

08:33.670 --> 08:35.880
I can't take it anymore.

08:37.880 --> 08:39.380
It's Annette.

08:39.380 --> 08:43.210
She keeps laying traps all over the place,

08:43.210 --> 08:45.630
and I keep getting caught in them.

08:46.210 --> 08:47.710
It just happened again.

08:56.830 --> 08:59.750
Yeep!

09:14.420 --> 09:16.000
Yeep, yeep, yeep!

09:18.380 --> 09:19.380
Yeep.

09:20.630 --> 09:22.080
How unlucky.

09:22.710 --> 09:26.830
Ah, I hear that was a problem at her academy, too.

09:26.830 --> 09:28.380
She got good grades,

09:28.380 --> 09:31.500
but she kept messing around and
building bizarre spy tools.

09:31.670 --> 09:39.000
Surely, she's just setting the traps
to make Teach say "I surrender," right?

09:39.000 --> 09:40.750
No way.

09:40.750 --> 09:43.670
She's doing it to torment me
so she can have a laugh.

09:43.670 --> 09:45.330
She's dead to me!

09:45.880 --> 09:47.290
Let's tail her.

09:47.290 --> 09:49.880
It shouldn't be hard to get to the bottom of this.

09:55.210 --> 09:57.920
I don't know why, but the carpet is bulging up.

09:58.920 --> 10:01.580
It is? I don't see any-

10:01.880 --> 10:03.130
I should step on it.

10:08.920 --> 10:10.130
How unlucky.

10:10.250 --> 10:11.500
I think I get it.

10:11.500 --> 10:12.710
Me too.

10:12.710 --> 10:16.380
She's just really susceptible to that sort of thing.

10:16.380 --> 10:19.290
If anything, I feel like she walked into that one.

10:19.290 --> 10:21.290
Not on purpose, but still.

10:21.460 --> 10:23.920
Wait, it's you again?!

10:23.920 --> 10:24.920
Yeep!

10:25.210 --> 10:26.830
That's annoying, yo.

10:26.830 --> 10:29.420
I want someone else to get caught for a change.

10:29.420 --> 10:32.000
How are you the person who's complaining here?!

10:32.130 --> 10:32.830
I hate you.

10:32.830 --> 10:33.670
It's probably six of one, half dozen of the other.
I hate you.<b></b>

10:33.670 --> 10:35.500
It's probably six of one, half dozen of the other.
I want an apology, now.<b></b>

10:35.500 --> 10:38.210
I don't think there's anything really to worry about.
Now you're just talking nonsense, yo.<b></b>

10:43.750 --> 10:45.710
The team's a mess.

10:45.710 --> 10:47.210
What do I do?

10:47.210 --> 10:49.790
At this rate, the Impossible Mission...

10:50.380 --> 10:51.750
is gonna wipe us all out?!

10:51.750 --> 10:53.750
I can't let that happen!

10:54.290 --> 10:56.880
Not when we've only just met,

10:56.880 --> 10:59.540
and not when I finally have a chance
to escape how things were

10:59.540 --> 11:02.330
and bloom into someone I can be proud of.

11:31.170 --> 11:32.920
Is that you, Grete?

11:33.380 --> 11:34.380
It is.

11:34.380 --> 11:36.460
I brought you some dinner, Boss.

11:36.460 --> 11:38.170
I see, thank you.

11:38.670 --> 11:40.880
You should head back to your room
and get some sleep.

11:40.880 --> 11:41.880
No, no.

11:41.880 --> 11:45.750
You must be tired from being out so late,
so I should at least serve you.

11:45.750 --> 11:47.710
I'm fine.
You should really go-

11:47.710 --> 11:48.920
Please let me in.

11:49.210 --> 11:50.830
I would very much like to serve you your dinner.

11:50.830 --> 11:54.210
You making it was already more than kind enough.

11:54.880 --> 11:56.080
Goodnight.

12:03.920 --> 12:06.420
Was he worried that I was going to attack him?

12:07.000 --> 12:11.790
I honestly just wanted to serve him dinner.

12:13.580 --> 12:19.380
Now that I think about it,
has Teach ever eaten a meal with us?

12:19.380 --> 12:20.630
He hasn't.

12:20.630 --> 12:24.960
He always cooks for one and eats alone in his room.

12:32.540 --> 12:36.790
You know, I've got a plan that
might just be worth trying.

12:40.380 --> 12:43.960
<b>FILE: Lamplight Days</b>

12:45.080 --> 12:46.330
I got trounced.

12:47.130 --> 12:51.080
I ran into Klaus at the firing range earlier,

12:51.080 --> 12:54.210
and he gave me some one-on-one coaching.

12:57.960 --> 12:59.630
Let's play Russian Roulette.

13:00.130 --> 13:02.420
I'll make you say, "I surrender," for sure.

13:02.420 --> 13:03.630
I'm game.

13:03.920 --> 13:05.880
Before we start, though...

13:07.130 --> 13:10.040
you should put that bullet you just
slipped out of the chamber back in.

13:10.830 --> 13:12.040
Put it back in.

13:12.670 --> 13:16.880
I actually challenged him as well.

13:25.500 --> 13:26.960
Want to keep going?

13:27.080 --> 13:29.540
Nah, I surrender.

13:30.130 --> 13:31.380
He got me good.

13:31.380 --> 13:35.750
With the way billiards works,
I was so sure I had it in the bag.

13:36.080 --> 13:39.710
Does that have something to do
with your special ability?

13:39.710 --> 13:42.500
The one you haven't told us about yet?

13:42.500 --> 13:45.830
If we take Teach on separately,
he's just going to crush us!

13:46.670 --> 13:51.130
That's why I, Wunderkind Lily, came up with a plan!

13:51.130 --> 13:52.330
"Wunderkind"?

13:52.330 --> 13:54.250
Just ignore that part.
Let her have it.

13:54.420 --> 13:59.540
But Wunderkind or not,
I won't be able to carry it out alone.

13:59.540 --> 14:01.790
I'm gonna need everyone's help.

14:02.210 --> 14:04.960
What do you say?
Will you lend me a hand?

14:06.670 --> 14:08.330
Not like we've got much of a choice, yeah?

14:08.330 --> 14:10.670
Seconded.
We all in?

14:10.670 --> 14:12.040
Let's do this!

14:12.630 --> 14:14.420
Then it's settled.

14:15.540 --> 14:19.670
Teach has a mission today,
so he'll be heading into town.

14:20.250 --> 14:21.580
When he does...

14:24.830 --> 14:26.040
This is Fool.

14:26.040 --> 14:28.630
The target stopped by a restaurant.

14:30.080 --> 14:31.330
This is Pandemonium.

14:32.000 --> 14:33.880
The target left the restaurant.

14:33.880 --> 14:35.330
Resuming pursuit.

14:54.460 --> 14:56.880
That figures, but we planned for this!

15:00.250 --> 15:01.710
This is Meadow.

15:01.710 --> 15:06.380
I told Mr. Bernard to stay far enough back
that Teach doesn't notice him.

15:06.830 --> 15:12.790
If we make him believe he gave us the slip,
even a pro's gonna let his guard down.

15:13.000 --> 15:17.250
B Team, use Mr. Bernard as a landmark
and follow Teach.

15:17.250 --> 15:18.250
Roger that.

15:18.830 --> 15:20.040
This is Daughter Dearest.

15:20.040 --> 15:22.580
According to one of the restaurant's employees,

15:22.580 --> 15:25.460
the boss has some foods he can't stand.

15:26.880 --> 15:27.880
And also...

15:28.210 --> 15:29.920
Oh hey, that's odd.

15:29.920 --> 15:32.290
That patron didn't finish his espresso.

15:32.500 --> 15:35.130
He might have had a stomachache.

15:35.130 --> 15:37.460
I saw him clutching at his belly.

15:43.080 --> 15:44.670
This is Dreamspeaker.

15:44.670 --> 15:48.250
The target is looking at some ingredients and frowning.

15:48.580 --> 15:49.880
This is Glint.

15:49.880 --> 15:51.960
The target boarded a train at the station.

15:51.960 --> 15:54.420
His mission today is probably in another town.

15:56.000 --> 15:57.460
All units, return to base.

15:57.460 --> 15:58.670
Send out the word!

15:58.670 --> 15:59.880
Aye aye!

16:03.210 --> 16:07.330
Thanks to everyone's hard work,
we were able to score some valuable intel.

16:08.080 --> 16:13.040
According to my hypothesis,
the reason Teach never eats with us...

16:13.040 --> 16:17.750
Is 'cuz he's got food allergies, yeah?

16:17.920 --> 16:20.460
Hey! Don't go stealing your leader's thunder!

16:20.880 --> 16:22.080
It does make sense.

16:22.080 --> 16:25.920
That's exactly the kind of information
a spy wouldn't want people to know.

16:25.920 --> 16:27.750
That checks out, yo!

16:27.750 --> 16:30.380
Then we'd better get started, Leader.

16:30.750 --> 16:31.960
A-hem!

16:32.330 --> 16:35.250
All right, everyone, let's get cooking!

16:35.250 --> 16:36.460
Yeah!

16:48.380 --> 16:50.630
Those are some fancy knife skills.

16:50.630 --> 16:53.460
Get out of my face.
You're in the way.

16:57.040 --> 16:59.460
Damn, I didn't know you were so handy in the kitchen.

16:59.460 --> 17:01.710
Cooking is a basic spy skill.

17:02.000 --> 17:04.790
For the tournée-cut carrots, do these look all right?

17:04.790 --> 17:06.170
That's brilliant.

17:06.540 --> 17:08.750
<i>Looks like everything's going smoothly over there.</i>

17:08.750 --> 17:10.920
<i>The problem is those two...</i>

17:11.670 --> 17:12.880
How's it coming?

17:12.880 --> 17:14.210
Don't talk to me.

17:14.210 --> 17:17.830
I have to be careful when I'm frying the shrimp.

17:17.830 --> 17:19.170
Got it!

17:19.170 --> 17:22.380
I've got a great tool to grind them up with, yo!

17:22.380 --> 17:24.210
Yeep?! That's ridiculous.

17:24.210 --> 17:27.500
Why do your inventions all have to be so destructive?

17:27.500 --> 17:30.000
Hey, you've got some sauce on your cheek.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.290
Here, let me get it.

17:31.290 --> 17:33.380
K-keep your hands to yourself!

17:34.540 --> 17:36.420
They'll be fine.

17:36.420 --> 17:40.420
Even when she acts mad like that,
she's actually enjoying herself.

17:40.420 --> 17:41.710
Yeah, I can tell.

17:42.630 --> 17:44.790
All right, you two, listen up!

17:45.960 --> 17:49.040
The others are almost done with the soup,

17:49.040 --> 17:52.500
so I was thinking we could get started
making a milk pudding to have for dessert.

17:52.500 --> 17:53.540
I'll help.

17:53.540 --> 17:55.250
Me too, yo!

17:57.500 --> 18:00.710
The two of them really are adorable.

18:00.710 --> 18:01.710
For sure.

18:02.040 --> 18:06.540
Hey, Lily, what gives?
You haven't been helpin' anyone.

18:06.710 --> 18:08.250
I'm the supervisor...

18:08.250 --> 18:10.210
or, like, the cheerleader?

18:11.250 --> 18:13.460
Get working, dammit!
Go set the table!

18:13.460 --> 18:15.960
Sybilla, the meat's burning.

18:15.960 --> 18:18.170
It's burning!

18:20.540 --> 18:23.710
You all made this for me?

18:23.710 --> 18:26.670
Yeah! We figured you'd be
tuckered out from your mission.

18:26.670 --> 18:29.000
Your subordinates cooked it for you
out of the goodness of their hearts

18:29.000 --> 18:30.920
and packed it full of love.

18:31.460 --> 18:33.000
Go on, dig in!

18:35.580 --> 18:37.460
<i>Based on what we learned from tailing him...</i>

18:37.460 --> 18:39.000
<i>...Klaus's weaknesses...</i>

18:39.000 --> 18:40.580
<i>...that is, the foods he avoids...</i>

18:40.580 --> 18:41.580
<i>...are beef...</i>

18:41.580 --> 18:44.000
<i>...shrimp, and anything with dairy!</i>

18:44.380 --> 18:45.750
<i>Come on, eat it.</i>

18:45.750 --> 18:46.960
<i>Eat it up, yo!</i>

18:46.960 --> 18:49.130
<i>Either that, or surrender!</i>

18:55.420 --> 18:56.670
Magnificent.

18:56.670 --> 18:59.170
That was just what I was craving.

18:59.500 --> 19:02.080
It... It was to your liking, Boss?

19:05.420 --> 19:06.460
It was.

19:06.630 --> 19:07.830
Thank goodness!

19:07.830 --> 19:09.960
Hold up, that ain't good at all!

19:14.750 --> 19:16.460
What the hell's goin' on here?!

19:16.460 --> 19:18.080
He pulled one over on us.

19:18.080 --> 19:19.880
He knew everything we were up to.

19:19.880 --> 19:21.790
All those things we learned while tailing him...

19:21.790 --> 19:23.710
...were stuff he wanted us to find out.

19:23.710 --> 19:27.670
That conversation those waiters had
was probably his doing, too.

19:30.880 --> 19:32.080
What do we do now?

19:32.080 --> 19:34.460
We got carried away and cooked way too much food.

19:35.960 --> 19:38.710
Ooh! I'm starving, yo!

19:38.960 --> 19:40.460
I'm hungry, too.

19:44.960 --> 19:47.040
<i>Taking into account what I learned today,</i>

19:47.040 --> 19:49.330
<i>the best way to split up the team
would be into those three groups.</i>

19:53.170 --> 19:55.420
<i>Meals are something you eat with your family.</i>

19:55.790 --> 19:59.460
<i>The more you share the same table,
the deeper your bonds grow.</i>

20:02.080 --> 20:04.750
I really screwed the pooch on this one...

20:04.750 --> 20:06.790
Don't be so hard on yourself.

20:06.790 --> 20:08.580
She's right, Leader.

20:08.580 --> 20:09.790
You mean it?

20:09.790 --> 20:12.580
You're really accepting someone like me
as your leader?

20:12.580 --> 20:15.210
Yeah, basically.
I mean, Klaus did appoint you.

20:15.750 --> 20:18.580
That guy pisses me the hell off!
The way he's always so goddamn composed...

20:18.580 --> 20:20.330
I mean, how old is he even?

20:20.330 --> 20:21.580
I actually know this one.

20:21.580 --> 20:24.540
I asked him when we were out shopping together.

20:24.540 --> 20:25.750
And?

20:26.000 --> 20:27.750
He's twenty.

20:28.630 --> 20:30.040
Shit, for real?

20:30.040 --> 20:32.830
That's basically the same age as us.

20:32.830 --> 20:35.670
In that case, I have an idea.

20:35.670 --> 20:38.080
Yeah, I just thought up a plan, too.

20:38.080 --> 20:41.040
I've got a special new creation up my sleeve for this!

20:41.460 --> 20:45.670
This time, we'll make Teach surrender for sure!

20:45.670 --> 20:47.040
Together, as a team!

20:47.040 --> 20:49.460
Let's do this!
Yeep!<b></b>

20:51.210 --> 20:55.330
<i>I expect they'll be spending the evening in high spirits
strengthening their bonds with each other.</i>

20:56.250 --> 20:58.750
<i>It will be cozy, like a family.</i>

21:00.040 --> 21:04.580
<i>But my family, Inferno, is gone.</i>

21:05.460 --> 21:09.920
<i>Now, I've lost my reason to share a table with people.</i>

21:11.790 --> 21:14.290
Hey, Leader, do you have a minute?

21:14.290 --> 21:16.290
Yup! Coming!

21:16.290 --> 21:18.210
Leader...

21:18.250 --> 21:19.540
You called?

21:19.830 --> 21:20.420
Leader!

21:20.420 --> 21:21.040
Leader!
Leader!<b></b>

21:21.040 --> 21:21.750
Leader!

21:21.750 --> 21:22.460
Leader!
Leader!<b></b>

21:22.460 --> 21:23.460
Leader!

21:23.460 --> 21:25.250
On it, on it, on it!

21:27.460 --> 21:30.920
A trusty leader's day starts early,
and the work never ends.

21:31.250 --> 21:34.630
From the way you're acting,
I guess you managed to quash your worries.

21:34.630 --> 21:37.420
Huh? I was worried about something?

21:39.460 --> 21:40.790
What's with that look?

21:40.790 --> 21:42.380
You got something you wanna say?

21:43.330 --> 21:44.330
No...

21:44.330 --> 21:45.920
Never change, Lily.

21:46.380 --> 21:49.250
That indominable spirit of yours is your greatest virtue.

21:49.250 --> 21:50.670
You know it!

21:50.670 --> 21:53.960
I'm gonna indomitably herald a new era.

21:54.420 --> 21:58.330
With Wunderkind Lily at its head,
Lamplight's going to lead the charge.

21:58.330 --> 22:00.500
I would expect nothing less.

22:02.080 --> 22:04.250
Make sure you all train hard today.

22:04.250 --> 22:06.460
Our inaugural Impossible Mission
is just around the corner.

22:07.420 --> 22:08.630
You got it!
